        "content": "<p>xixi-box opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15285\">PR #15285</a> from <code>xixi-box:fix/issue-15277-5d042ce-c9d671a3</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #15277</p>\n<p>Root cause: A call return PC can equal the following interrupt_poll fault PC, causing distinct user stack maps to share an address and violate their strict ordering; inserting a NOP before the poll when these PCs collide preserves both maps.</p>\n<p>&lt;!-- oss-scout-job:job-9193e006-1300-423c-9dd2-c9d671a305f3 --&gt;</p>\n<p>Tests: <code>target/debug/clif-util test -v cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/interrupt-poll-after-call.clif</code> (fails on base; passes with this patch).<br>\nRegression coverage: <code>cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/interrupt-poll-after-call.clif</code>.</p>\n<p>AI assistance: Codex helped implement and test this change. oss-scout independently replayed the regression before opening this PR.</p>\n</blockquote>",
